#
# For each of the three matrix products, we:
#   - Fission the inner (i,j) loop to separate initialization from
#     the k-loop.
#   - Reorder the j and k loops so that j is innermost.
#
# This reordering makes the accesses B[k, j], D[k, j], and F[k, j]
# traverse contiguous memory in j, improving cache behavior. The
# reductions are associative and Exo’s analysis verifies correctness.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

